WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.650
Welcome back to Learn Text.js.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.700
This is chapter ten,
the last one: Shipping.

3
00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:11.490
Acme Deploys is ready to ship.

4
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:13.580
First, build it.

5
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.296
bun run build runs text build.

6
00:00:16.344 --> 00:00:18.480
It produces a static client,

7
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:23.030
and because the app has a route
handler, a server for text start.

8
00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:28.990
The route table lists every page, and
the route handler at /api/deployments.

9
00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.230
text start serves the build
and runs your route handlers.

10
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:37.560
It runs on any host with Bun
1.2 or Node 22 and later.

11
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:42.320
Next, metadata.

12
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:49.230
The browser tab is the only pixel of
chrome your app has, so give it a title.

13
00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:53.630
The root layout from the routing chapter
sets a default title and a template.

14
00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:55.990
A page can export its own metadata,

15
00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:00.720
and with the template, the
tab reads Deployments · Acme.

16
00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.440
Now, static hosting.

17
00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.910
Without route handlers, the
build is a plain static site.

18
00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.910
Each static route gets its own HTML file,

19
00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:20.510
and dynamic routes like /deployments/[id]
are served by index.html.

20
00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.830
On Vercel and Cloudflare Pages,

21
00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:26.510
text build detects the platform
and sets that up itself.

22
00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.830
Other static hosts need a rewrite.

23
00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:32.830
On Netlify, it's one line
in public/_redirects.

24
00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:35.430
Netlify serves files that exist first,

25
00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:39.200
so assets and prerendered
routes are unaffected.

26
00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:44.600
Before you ship, three checks.

27
00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:50.710
Turn off Preserve log in your console
settings, and tell your users to do the same.

28
00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:55.790
Test at 80 by 24, because someone
will dock DevTools to the side.

29
00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.280
And run bun test.

30
00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:01.670
Here it is on the lesson page.

31
00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:06.710
Click the pad first, so the page
has focus, then press Enter to ship.

32
00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:12.310
text build runs, then vercel deploy uploads
the project and Vercel runs the build.

33
00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.080
Acme Deploys is live.

34
00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:18.670
Quick check.

35
00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:22.480
What does a static host
need for dynamic routes?

36
00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:26.630
A rewrite to index.html.

37
00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:30.390
Static routes are prerendered
to their own HTML files.

38
00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:35.480
Dynamic segments fall back to
the client app in index.html.

39
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:39.880
And which console setting should be off?

40
00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.730
Preserve log.

41
00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:48.780
Text.js clears the console to release
old frames, and Preserve log keeps them.

42
00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.730
That's the course.

43
00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:56.930
Your certificate is at
textjs.org/learn/certificate.

44
00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:01.140
Add your name, and it's printed
on the page and in your console.
